From 62c90b6d51de6e19ccd0c2d163cf3c1a64545663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:33:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(sandbox): skills mount/sync withhold read-denied
 files; case-insensitive read deny-list

The skills bind mount shipped a symlink-free skills/ raw, including skills/.hub
(prompt-injection cache) and skill .env/.env.local/.envrc files the read guard
blocks; per-file sync pruned .hub but still uploaded .env-type files.

- _walk_skill_tree full-checks its root and every entry whose name is a
  read-deny candidate (read_deny_candidate_names: rule names + resolved target
  basenames, so symlinked stores are caught), fail-closed.
- Mount: symlinks, .hub or any denied entry force the sanitized copy, now one
  per source dir, refreshed in place (atomic os.replace, ns mtime) instead of
  rmtree+mkdtemp, which emptied live containers' mounts and let a second root
  delete the first root's copy.
- get_read_block_error compares casefolded (AUTH.JSON / .HUB on macOS opened the
  denied file); resolves the skills/.hub base. Over-blocks case variants on
  case-sensitive FS by design. Write guards are unchanged (follow-up).
